<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anastasius I Dicorus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 430–518</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> · Also known as Anastasius I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anastasius I was emperor of the Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> from 491 to 518. A palace official chosen by the widowed empress <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ariadne">Ariadne</a>, he reformed the coinage and taxation, leaving a large surplus in the treasury, and fought a war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> from 502 to 506. His sympathy for Miaphysite views provoked revolts, and his treaty of around 502 made the Ghassanids the empire's leading Arab allies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anastasius-i-dicorus.jpg" alt="Anastasius I Dicorus" width="320" height="312" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anastasius_I._minted_507-518.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
